				<content:encoded><![CDATA[<p>We all know <strong>Madonna</strong> will perform at the next <strong>Grammy Awards</strong> on February 8, and we are so excited!<br />
To celebrate this great news we have decided to create a poll and choose the best performance of the Queen during the past edition of the Grammys.<br />
Surprisingly, <strong>Madonna</strong> didn’t take to the stage until her 1999 Geisha-inspired performance of “<strong>Nothing Really Matters</strong>” at the 41st ceremony, where she also took home three awards. Two years later, her Holy Madgesty kicked off the 43rd annual show by driving onto the stage in a leather jacket with Lil Bow Wow to perform “<strong>Music</strong>.” A few years later, she returned with a truly innovative concept: Virtual reality! Madge paired with animated troupe Gorillaz for a mash-up of “Feel Good Inc.” and lead Confessions dance floor anthem, “<strong>Hung Up</strong>.” And most recently, Madonna arrived to the stage during last year’s show alongside Macklemore and Queen Latifah to mass-marry a ton of gay couples live while performing “<strong>Open Your Heart</strong>” and “Same Love.”<br />
And now? We are really eager to see what will happen on that stage!<br />
Watch all the performances below and then cast your vote!<br />
